      "stadium.text.medicham.honest": "Its win% does not beat a coin. On the held-out fifth the live in-game leaf is <em>worse</em> than a coin on Brier — paired +0.0502, 95% CI [0.0371, 0.0628], where lower is better — and it names the winner on 51.0% of 1,314 decisive calls, 95% CI [48.3, 53.7], an interval that contains chance, with ECE 0.1811 (<code>data/winrate-backtest.json</code>). This cabinet previously read <s class='wd' title='Withdrawn 2026-08-04 — the 2026-07-23 reading, superseded by data/winrate-backtest.json measured 2026-08-04, which puts accuracy at 51.0% with a CI containing 50%.'>log-loss 1.2 against 0.69 and ~44% of decisive calls, which is below chance and therefore systematically inverted</s>; the current artifact does not support the inversion, so it is struck out here rather than quietly deleted. The damage math is validated. The win probability is a matchup heuristic wearing a probability's clothes.",
